---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Documentation — Morflow Data Processing Engine"
  description="Comprehensive step-by-step technical guide for the Morflow CLI and the .morf dataflow pipeline syntax."
  path="/doc"
>
  <PageHero
    badge="Documentation"
  >
    Morflow Engine &amp; <em>Syntax Reference</em>
  </PageHero>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <!-- Sticky Sidebar -->
    <aside class="docs-sidebar" aria-label="Documentation Navigation">
      <div class="docs-nav-group">
        <a href="#cli" class="docs-nav-title">1. CLI Reference</a>
        <ul class="docs-nav-list">
          <li><a href="#cli-installation" class="docs-nav-link">1.1. Installation</a></li>
          <li><a href="#cli-commands" class="docs-nav-link">1.2. Core CLI Commands</a></li>
          <li><a href="#cli-check" class="docs-nav-link">1.3. Pipeline Verification (check)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#cli-prep" class="docs-nav-link">1.4. Offline Prep (prep)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#cli-search-spec" class="docs-nav-link">1.5. Search &amp; Spec</a></li>
          <li><a href="#cli-env" class="docs-nav-link">1.6. Environment Variables</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="docs-nav-group">
        <a href="#syntax" class="docs-nav-title">2. .morf Syntax Guide</a>
        <ul class="docs-nav-list">
          <li><a href="#syntax-step1-action" class="docs-nav-link">2.1. Anatomy of an Action</a></li>
          <li><a href="#syntax-step2-flow" class="docs-nav-link">2.2. Inputs &amp; Constructing a Flow</a></li>
          <li><a href="#syntax-step3-emit" class="docs-nav-link">2.3. Emitting Output &amp; Intermediate Emission (emit)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#syntax-step4-multiflow" class="docs-nav-link">2.4. Multiple Flows in One File</a></li>
          <li><a href="#syntax-step5-control" class="docs-nav-link">2.5. Advanced Control Flow (Loops &amp; Conditionals)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#syntax-step6-examples" class="docs-nav-link">2.6. Complete End-to-End Examples</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="docs-nav-group">
        <a href="#types" class="docs-nav-title">3. Data Types &amp; Type System</a>
        <ul class="docs-nav-list">
          <li><a href="#types-overview" class="docs-nav-link">3.1. Type Hierarchy &amp; Architecture</a></li>
          <li><a href="#types-tensor" class="docs-nav-link">3.2. Tensor (Tensor)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#types-image" class="docs-nav-link">3.3. Image (Image)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#types-audio" class="docs-nav-link">3.4. Audio (Audio)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#types-scalar" class="docs-nav-link">3.5. Scalar (Scalar)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#types-rawbytes" class="docs-nav-link">3.6. RawBytes (RawBytes)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#types-composite" class="docs-nav-link">3.7. Composite (Composite)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#types-arguments" class="docs-nav-link">3.8. Configuration Arguments (*Arg)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#types-each" class="docs-nav-link">3.9. Deep Dive: Slicing &amp; Restacking with 'each'</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="docs-nav-group">
        <a href="#exec" class="docs-nav-title">4. Pipeline Execution</a>
        <ul class="docs-nav-list">
          <li><a href="#exec-python" class="docs-nav-link">4.1. Python</a></li>
          <li><a href="#exec-js" class="docs-nav-link">4.2. JavaScript / Node.js</a></li>
          <li><a href="#exec-java" class="docs-nav-link">4.3. Java</a></li>
          <li><a href="#exec-rust" class="docs-nav-link">4.4. Rust</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <article class="docs-content">
      <!-- SECTION 1: CLI REFERENCE -->
      <section id="cli" class="doc-section">
        <div class="doc-section-header">
          <p class="badge">Section 1</p>
          <h2 class="doc-h2">1. CLI Reference</h2>
          <p class="doc-p">
            The <code>morflow</code> CLI handles dependency resolution, offline action caching, action discovery, and action specification inspection.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="cli-installation" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">1.1. Installation</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            Install the standalone <code>morflow</code> command-line interface globally via cURL, npm, or pip:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>CLI Installation</span>
              <span>Shell</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Install standalone native binary via cURL</span>
curl -fsSL https://morflow.org/install.sh | bash

<span class="tok-comment"># Or install via NPM (Global CLI)</span>
npm install -g morflow

<span class="tok-comment"># Or install via Pip (Python CLI)</span>
pip install morflow</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="cli-commands" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">1.2. Core CLI Commands</h3>
          <div class="doc-table-container">
            <table class="doc-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Command</th>
                  <th>Syntax</th>
                  <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>check</code></td>
                  <td><code>morflow check &lt;file.morf&gt; [-p &lt;dir&gt;]</code></td>
                  <td>Validates syntax, verifies Single Static Assignment (SSA), inspects dynamic action FFI types, and performs a dry-run execution simulation.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>prep</code></td>
                  <td><code>morflow prep &lt;file.morf&gt; [-p &lt;dir&gt;] [-f]</code></td>
                  <td>Pre-downloads required actions for completely offline execution.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>search</code></td>
                  <td><code>morflow search &lt;query&gt; [-l &lt;limit&gt;]</code></td>
                  <td>Fuzzy searches actions in the central registry.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>spec</code></td>
                  <td><code>morflow spec &lt;pkg&gt;/&lt;ver&gt;/&lt;action&gt;</code></td>
                  <td>Inspects argument schemas, types, and action documentation.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>install</code></td>
                  <td><code>morflow install &lt;action&gt; [-p &lt;dir&gt;] [-f]</code></td>
                  <td>Installs a specific action binary directly into the cache.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>list</code></td>
                  <td><code>morflow list [-p &lt;dir&gt;]</code></td>
                  <td>Lists all installed action binaries in the local cache.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>clean</code></td>
                  <td><code>morflow clean [-p &lt;dir&gt;]</code></td>
                  <td>Removes cached action binaries from the action path.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="cli-check" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">1.3. Pipeline Verification (<code>check</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            The <code>check</code> command performs comprehensive static analysis, type checking, and shape inference on your <code>.morf</code> pipeline without requiring live input data. It guarantees that syntax, Single Static Assignment (SSA) rules, action binaries, flowable types, and tensor dimensions are 100% valid before deployment:
          </p>
          <ul class="doc-list" style="margin: 0 0 16px 20px; color: var(--grey-800); line-height: 1.65;">
            <li><strong>Type &amp; Parameter Validation:</strong> Verifies all declared parameter types, ensuring argument types (e.g. <code>IntArg</code>) are not piped as flow heads (preventing <code>E007</code>) and that actions receive matching inputs.</li>
            <li><strong>Shape Inference ABI:</strong> Evaluates action shape contracts (<code>get_output_shape</code>) across the dataflow graph to verify rank compatibility, wildcard dimensions (e.g. <code>Tensor[*, *]</code>), and channel derivations.</li>
            <li><strong>Reducer Axis Bounds Checking:</strong> Statically proves that reduction operations (e.g. <code>sum</code>, <code>mean</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>norm</code>, <code>argmax</code>) do not specify out-of-bounds axes against pinned tensor ranks (preventing <code>E010</code>).</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Pipeline Static Analysis &amp; Shape Verification</span>
              <span>Bash</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Verify pipeline syntax, action binaries, type safety, and tensor shapes</span>
morflow check ./pipeline.morf

<span class="tok-comment"># Check with a custom action cache directory</span>
morflow check ./pipeline.morf --path ./actions_cache</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="cli-prep" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">1.4. Offline Prep (<code>prep</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            In production deployments, you can ensure zero network requests at runtime by pre-downloading all action binaries during container image build:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Offline Action Preparation</span>
              <span>Bash</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Download required action binaries into local cache</span>
morflow prep ./pipeline.morf

<span class="tok-comment"># Force re-download even if action is already present</span>
morflow prep ./pipeline.morf --force

<span class="tok-comment"># Download action binaries into a custom directory</span>
morflow prep ./pipeline.morf --path ./actions_cache</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="cli-search-spec" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">1.5. Search &amp; Spec</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            Search for available actions and view their expected parameters directly in your terminal:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Action Discovery</span>
              <span>Bash</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Search for color or audio transformation actions</span>
morflow search color
morflow search biquad

<span class="tok-comment"># Inspect argument schemas and SPEC.md docs</span>
morflow spec image_essentials/latest/color_adjust
morflow spec audio_essentials/latest/biquad_filter</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="cli-env" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">1.6. Environment Variables</h3>
          <div class="doc-table-container">
            <table class="doc-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Variable</th>
                  <th>Default</th>
                  <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>MORFLOW_ACTIONS_PATH</code></td>
                  <td><code>~/.morflow/actions</code></td>
                  <td>Directory where Morflow caches and resolves compiled dynamic action libraries (<code>.so</code>, <code>.dylib</code>, <code>.dll</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>MORFLOW_REPO</code></td>
                  <td><code>JiraPit/Morflow</code></td>
                  <td>Target GitHub repository used by the CLI to query releases and download precompiled action binaries.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 2: MORF SYNTAX STEP-BY-STEP -->
      <section id="syntax" class="doc-section">
        <div class="doc-section-header">
          <p class="badge">Section 2</p>
          <h2 class="doc-h2">2. .morf Syntax Guide</h2>
          <p class="doc-p">
            Learn <code>.morf</code> syntax from the ground up: starting from the smallest building block (an <strong>Action</strong>), to chaining them into a <strong>Flow</strong>, producing results with <strong>Emit</strong>, and composing <strong>Multiple Flows</strong> in a single file.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 1: ANATOMY OF AN ACTION -->
        <div id="syntax-step1-action" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">2.1. Anatomy of an Action</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            An <strong>Action</strong> is the fundamental atomic unit of computation in Morflow. It represents an isolated, high-performance compiled operation (e.g. image resizing, Gaussian blur, audio biquad filtering, tensor normalization).
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            Actions can be invoked in three main forms:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Action Invocation Forms</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Form 1: Zero-argument actions (parentheses are optional)</span>
<span class="tok-fn">to_image</span>
<span class="tok-fn">to_wav</span>
<span class="tok-fn">identity</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># Form 2: Keyword arguments (key=value)</span>
<span class="tok-fn">resize</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-num">512</span>, <span class="tok-param">height</span>=<span class="tok-num">512</span>, <span class="tok-param">filter</span>=<span class="tok-str">"bilinear"</span>)
<span class="tok-fn">color_adjust</span>(<span class="tok-param">contrast</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.15</span>, <span class="tok-param">saturation</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.05</span>, <span class="tok-param">brightness</span>=<span class="tok-num">0.02</span>)
<span class="tok-fn">biquad_filter</span>(<span class="tok-param">type</span>=<span class="tok-str">"highpass"</span>, <span class="tok-param">freq</span>=<span class="tok-num">30.0</span>, <span class="tok-param">sample_rate</span>=<span class="tok-num">48000</span>)

<span class="tok-comment"># Form 3: Variable arguments (passing pipeline parameters to action parameters)</span>
<span class="tok-fn">resize</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-var">$target_width</span>, <span class="tok-param">height</span>=<span class="tok-var">$target_height</span>)
<span class="tok-fn">resample</span>(<span class="tok-param">to_rate</span>=<span class="tok-var">$target_sample_rate</span>)</code></pre>
          </div>

          <p class="doc-p">
            Before using actions, import their parent <strong>Action Pack</strong> at the top of your <code>.morf</code> file:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Importing Actions</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Package-level import (brings actions into scope or under an alias)</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> base/latest
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> audio_essentials/latest <span class="tok-keyword">as</span> audio

<span class="tok-comment"># Item import (brings specific actions into local scope)</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">from</span> image_essentials/latest <span class="tok-keyword">import</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_tensor</span>, <span class="tok-fn">resize</span>, <span class="tok-fn">color_adjust</span>, <span class="tok-fn">gaussian_blur</span>, <span class="tok-fn">to_image</span></code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 2: CONSTRUCTING A FLOW -->
        <div id="syntax-step2-flow" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">2.2. Inputs &amp; Constructing a Flow</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            A <strong>Flow</strong> connects an input variable through a sequence of actions using the <code>&gt;&gt;</code> dataflow operator. Each action receives the output payload of the previous action with zero memory copying.
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            Inputs and configurable parameters are declared using <code>accept</code> at the top of the file:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Declaring Pipeline Inputs</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Declare flowable input payload</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Image</span> <span class="tok-var">$img_in</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># Declare configuration arguments with defaults</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">IntArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$target_width</span> = <span class="tok-num">512</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">IntArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$target_height</span> = <span class="tok-num">512</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">BoolArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$normalize</span> = <span class="tok-keyword">true</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-callout">
            <strong>Data Types &amp; Dimensions:</strong> Morflow pipelines use an explicit typed parameter model (<code>Tensor</code>, <code>Image</code>, <code>Audio</code>, <code>Scalar</code>, <code>RawBytes</code>, and <code>*Arg</code>). For a complete walkthrough of every data type, shape declaration syntax, and how types behave under parallel slicing, see <a href="#types" style="color: var(--brand-500); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">Section 3: Data Types &amp; Type System</a>.
          </div>

          <p class="doc-p" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            Once inputs and parameters are declared, chain actions into a continuous dataflow stream:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>A Sequential Flow Chain</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># The flow starts with the flowable input $img_in and passes data step-by-step</span>
<span class="tok-var">$img_in</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_tensor</span>(<span class="tok-param">color</span>=<span class="tok-str">"rgb"</span>, <span class="tok-param">dtype</span>=<span class="tok-str">"f32"</span>, <span class="tok-param">layout</span>=<span class="tok-str">"hwc"</span>, <span class="tok-param">normalize</span>=<span class="tok-var">$normalize</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">resize</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-var">$target_width</span>, <span class="tok-param">height</span>=<span class="tok-var">$target_height</span>, <span class="tok-param">filter</span>=<span class="tok-str">"bilinear"</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">color_adjust</span>(<span class="tok-param">contrast</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.15</span>, <span class="tok-param">saturation</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.05</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">gaussian_blur</span>(<span class="tok-param">sigma</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.2</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_image</span>(<span class="tok-param">color</span>=<span class="tok-str">"rgba"</span>, <span class="tok-param">dtype</span>=<span class="tok-str">"u8"</span>)</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 3: EMITTING OUTPUT -->
        <div id="syntax-step3-emit" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">2.3. Emitting Output &amp; Intermediate Emission (<code>emit</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            Outputs are transferred back to the calling host application across many platforms and languages using the <code>emit</code> keyword. Importantly, <strong><code>emit</code> is a non-terminating passthrough operation</strong> — it yields the computed payload at that point in execution while passing the data directly down the chain for subsequent operations.
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            This enables <strong>intermediate emission</strong>, allowing a single continuous flow to dispatch checkpoints, previews, or multi-scale outputs without duplicating upstream work or branching into separate pipelines:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Intermediate Emission & Chaining</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Form A: Single primary emission</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> base/latest
<span class="tok-keyword">from</span> base/latest <span class="tok-keyword">import</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_tensor</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">from</span> image_essentials/latest <span class="tok-keyword">import</span> <span class="tok-fn">resize</span>

<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Image</span> <span class="tok-var">$img_in</span>
<span class="tok-var">$img_in</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_tensor</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">resize</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-num">512</span>, <span class="tok-param">height</span>=<span class="tok-num">512</span>) <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># Form B: Named stream emission</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> audio_essentials/latest

<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">RawBytes</span> <span class="tok-var">$audio_in</span>
<span class="tok-var">$audio_in</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_audio</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">normalize</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span>(<span class="tok-str">"normalized_audio"</span>)

<span class="tok-comment"># Form C: Intermediate emission with chained downstream processing</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> base/latest
<span class="tok-keyword">from</span> base/latest <span class="tok-keyword">import</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_tensor</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">from</span> image_essentials/latest <span class="tok-keyword">import</span> <span class="tok-fn">resize</span>, <span class="tok-fn">color_adjust</span>

<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Image</span> <span class="tok-var">$img_in</span>
<span class="tok-var">$img_in</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_tensor</span>(<span class="tok-param">color</span>=<span class="tok-str">"rgb"</span>, <span class="tok-param">normalize</span>=<span class="tok-keyword">true</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">resize</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-num">1024</span>, <span class="tok-param">height</span>=<span class="tok-num">1024</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span>(<span class="tok-str">"high_res"</span>)               <span class="tok-comment"># Emits intermediate 1024x1024 tensor to host</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">resize</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-num">256</span>, <span class="tok-param">height</span>=<span class="tok-num">256</span>)   <span class="tok-comment"># Continues stream without re-ingesting $img_in</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">color_adjust</span>(<span class="tok-param">contrast</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.2</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span>(<span class="tok-str">"preview"</span>)                <span class="tok-comment"># Emits downstream preview thumbnail</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-callout">
            <strong>Host Return Type & Multi-Emission:</strong> When a flow contains multiple or named emissions (such as intermediate emissions), host SDKs receive a structured dictionary or map of typed outputs (e.g. <code>dict[str, np.ndarray]</code> in Python, <code>Map&lt;String, MorflowTensor&gt;</code> in Java, or <code>MorflowOutput</code> in Rust). For streaming invocations, intermediate emissions can also be consumed asynchronously as they are produced.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 4: MULTIPLE FLOWS IN ONE FILE -->
        <div id="syntax-step4-multiflow" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">2.4. Multiple Flows in One File</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            A single <code>.morf</code> file can contain <strong>multiple flows</strong>. You can capture intermediate states mid-stream into a tapped variable using <code>&gt;&gt; $var_name</code>, and then spawn independent branch flows from that variable.
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            Morflow automatically compiles all flows into an acyclic dependency graph (DAG) and executes non-dependent branches concurrently across multi-threaded CPU cores with zero lock overhead:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Multi-Flow Audio Split Pipeline</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-keyword">import</span> audio_essentials/latest
 
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">RawBytes</span> <span class="tok-var">$input_audio</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># FLOW 1: Ingest input audio, convert to structured stream, and tap into $decoded</span>
<span class="tok-var">$input_audio</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_audio</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-var">$decoded</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># FLOW 2: Extract channel 0 (Left), apply low-pass filtering, convert to WAV, and emit</span>
<span class="tok-var">$decoded</span>[0] <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">biquad_filter</span>(<span class="tok-param">type</span>=<span class="tok-str">"lowpass"</span>, <span class="tok-param">freq</span>=<span class="tok-num">1200.0</span>) <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_wav</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span>(<span class="tok-str">"left_filtered"</span>)

<span class="tok-comment"># FLOW 3: Extract channel 1 (Right), apply high-pass filtering, convert to WAV, and emit</span>
<span class="tok-var">$decoded</span>[1] <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">biquad_filter</span>(<span class="tok-param">type</span>=<span class="tok-str">"highpass"</span>, <span class="tok-param">freq</span>=<span class="tok-num">800.0</span>) <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_wav</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span>(<span class="tok-str">"right_filtered"</span>)</code></pre>
          </div>

          <p class="doc-p">
            In this pipeline, <strong>Flow 2 and Flow 3 run concurrently in parallel</strong> immediately after Flow 1 finishes. Because both downstream branches depend solely on the shared output of Flow 1 (<code>$decoded</code>) but have no dependency on each other, Morflow's runtime automatically schedules and evaluates them simultaneously across CPU worker threads with zero lock overhead.
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Static Single Assignment (SSA) Rule:</strong> A tapped variable identifier (e.g. <code>$decoded</code>) cannot be reassigned or mutated within the same scope. This mathematical guarantee ensures safe multi-threaded memory buffer sharing without copy overhead.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 5: LOOPS & CONDITIONALS -->
        <div id="syntax-step5-control" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">2.5. Advanced Control Flow (Loops &amp; Conditionals)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            Morflow includes built-in constructs for parallel loops, conditional branching, and pattern routing within flows:
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Parallel Map Loop (<code>each</code>):</strong> The <code>each</code> block applies a transformation sub-flow across elements of a collection, batch, or multi-channel audio/image tensor. <strong>Each iteration is executed concurrently in parallel</strong> across multi-threaded CPU workers. Once all parallel iterations complete, their resulting outputs are automatically <strong>stacked back together</strong> in sequence order and passed directly to the next action in the stream.
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Parallel Map Loop (each)</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-keyword">import</span> audio_essentials/latest

<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">RawBytes</span> <span class="tok-var">$input_audio</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># Iterates each channel concurrently in parallel, transforms, and stacks back together</span>
<span class="tok-var">$input_audio</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_audio</span>(<span class="tok-param">sample_rate</span>=<span class="tok-num">44100</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-keyword">each</span> (<span class="tok-var">$channel</span>) &#123;
        <span class="tok-var">$channel</span>
            <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">biquad_filter</span>(<span class="tok-param">type</span>=<span class="tok-str">"highpass"</span>, <span class="tok-param">freq</span>=<span class="tok-num">30.0</span>, <span class="tok-param">sample_rate</span>=<span class="tok-num">48000</span>)
            <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">compressor</span>(<span class="tok-param">threshold_db</span>=<span class="tok-num">-12.0</span>, <span class="tok-param">ratio</span>=<span class="tok-num">3.0</span>)
    &#125;
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">stereo_widen</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.2</span>)   <span class="tok-comment"># Receives the stacked multi-channel stream</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_wav</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-callout">
            <strong>Emission Rule for Loops:</strong> Direct emission (<code>emit</code>) inside an <code>each</code> block is strictly <strong>not allowed</strong>. Because loop iterations execute concurrently and asynchronously out-of-order, emissions must be performed outside the <code>each</code> block on the aggregated and stacked stream to maintain deterministic host synchronization and graph integrity.
          </div>

          <p class="doc-p" style="margin-top: 24px;">
            <strong>Conditionals &amp; Dynamic Routing:</strong> Branch pipelines conditionally based on runtime metadata or route streams dynamically:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Conditionals &amp; Dynamic Routing</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-keyword">import</span> audio_essentials/latest

<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">RawBytes</span> <span class="tok-var">$input_audio</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">IntArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$sample_rate</span> = <span class="tok-num">44100</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">IntArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$channels</span> = <span class="tok-num">2</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 1. If / Else branching</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">if</span> (<span class="tok-var">$sample_rate</span> != <span class="tok-num">48000</span>) &#123;
    <span class="tok-var">$input_audio</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">resample</span>(<span class="tok-param">to_rate</span>=<span class="tok-num">48000</span>) <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-var">$prepared</span>
&#125; <span class="tok-keyword">else</span> &#123;
    <span class="tok-var">$input_audio</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-var">$prepared</span>
&#125;

<span class="tok-comment"># 2. Dynamic route pattern matching</span>
<span class="tok-var">$prepared</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-keyword">route</span> &#123;
    <span class="tok-var">$channels</span> == <span class="tok-num">1</span> =&gt; <span class="tok-fn">biquad_filter</span>(<span class="tok-param">type</span>=<span class="tok-str">"lowpass"</span>, <span class="tok-param">freq</span>=<span class="tok-num">1000.0</span>)
    <span class="tok-var">$channels</span> == <span class="tok-num">2</span> =&gt; <span class="tok-fn">stereo_widen</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.4</span>)
    <span class="tok-keyword">else</span> =&gt; <span class="tok-fn">identity</span>
&#125; <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_wav</span> <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span></code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 6: COMPLETE EXAMPLES -->
        <div id="syntax-step6-examples" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">2.6. Complete End-to-End Examples</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            Here are two complete, production-ready <code>.morf</code> pipeline definitions:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Complete Vision Pipeline</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Morflow Image Processing Pipeline (.morf)</span>

<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> base/latest
<span class="tok-keyword">from</span> base/latest <span class="tok-keyword">import</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_tensor</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">from</span> image_essentials/latest <span class="tok-keyword">import</span> <span class="tok-fn">resize</span>, <span class="tok-fn">color_adjust</span>, <span class="tok-fn">gaussian_blur</span>, <span class="tok-fn">to_image</span>

<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Image</span> <span class="tok-var">$img_in</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">IntArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$target_width</span> = <span class="tok-num">512</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">IntArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$target_height</span> = <span class="tok-num">512</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># Direct chained dataflow from host image input to emitted output</span>
<span class="tok-var">$img_in</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_tensor</span>(<span class="tok-param">color</span>=<span class="tok-str">"rgb"</span>, <span class="tok-param">dtype</span>=<span class="tok-str">"f32"</span>, <span class="tok-param">layout</span>=<span class="tok-str">"hwc"</span>, <span class="tok-param">normalize</span>=<span class="tok-keyword">true</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">resize</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-var">$target_width</span>, <span class="tok-param">height</span>=<span class="tok-var">$target_height</span>, <span class="tok-param">filter</span>=<span class="tok-str">"bilinear"</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">color_adjust</span>(<span class="tok-param">contrast</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.15</span>, <span class="tok-param">saturation</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.05</span>, <span class="tok-param">brightness</span>=<span class="tok-num">0.02</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">gaussian_blur</span>(<span class="tok-param">sigma</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.2</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_image</span>(<span class="tok-param">color</span>=<span class="tok-str">"rgba"</span>, <span class="tok-param">dtype</span>=<span class="tok-str">"u8"</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Complete Audio DSP Pipeline</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Morflow Audio DSP Pipeline (.morf)</span>

<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> audio_essentials/latest

<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">RawBytes</span> <span class="tok-var">$input_audio</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">IntArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$sample_rate</span> = <span class="tok-num">44100</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># Direct chained DSP processing with inline multi-channel loop</span>
<span class="tok-var">$input_audio</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_audio</span>(<span class="tok-param">sample_rate</span>=<span class="tok-var">$sample_rate</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">resample</span>(<span class="tok-param">to_rate</span>=<span class="tok-num">48000</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">normalize</span>(<span class="tok-param">target_peak</span>=<span class="tok-num">0.95</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-keyword">each</span> (<span class="tok-var">$channel</span>) &#123;
        <span class="tok-var">$channel</span>
            <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">biquad_filter</span>(<span class="tok-param">type</span>=<span class="tok-str">"highpass"</span>, <span class="tok-param">freq</span>=<span class="tok-num">30.0</span>, <span class="tok-param">sample_rate</span>=<span class="tok-num">48000</span>)
            <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">compressor</span>(<span class="tok-param">threshold_db</span>=<span class="tok-num">-12.0</span>, <span class="tok-param">ratio</span>=<span class="tok-num">3.0</span>)
    &#125;
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">stereo_widen</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.2</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">limiter</span>(<span class="tok-param">ceiling_db</span>=<span class="tok-num">-0.1</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_wav</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span></code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 3: DATA TYPES & TYPE SYSTEM -->
      <section id="types" class="doc-section">
        <div class="doc-section-header">
          <p class="badge">Section 3</p>
          <h2 class="doc-h2">3. Data Types &amp; Type System</h2>
          <p class="doc-p">
            Morflow features an explicit, compile-time verified type system and shape algebra. Every input parameter accepted by a pipeline and every payload streaming through <code>&gt;&gt;</code> flows carries a verifiable type and rank constraint, enabling static validation and zero train-serve skew without runtime execution overhead.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 3.1: TYPE HIERARCHY -->
        <div id="types-overview" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">3.1. Type Hierarchy &amp; Architecture</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            Types in Morflow are fundamentally divided into two distinct classes:
          </p>
          <ul class="doc-list" style="margin: 0 0 16px 20px; color: var(--grey-800); line-height: 1.65;">
            <li>
              <strong>Flowable Payloads:</strong> High-performance multi-dimensional arrays, signals, images, or byte buffers that stream through <code>&gt;&gt;</code> dataflow chains, participate in parallel <code>each</code> loops, and can be yielded to the host via <code>emit</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Configuration Arguments (<code>*Arg</code>):</strong> Parameter values passed from host applications to configure action arguments (such as image resolutions, filter cutoffs, or sample rates). Arguments <em>cannot</em> be piped as the head of a flow (preventing compile error <code>E007</code>).
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div class="doc-table-container">
            <table class="doc-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Type</th>
                  <th>Classification</th>
                  <th>Default / Shape Syntax</th>
                  <th>Can Stream (<code>&gt;&gt;</code>)</th>
                  <th>Iterated by <code>each</code></th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Tensor</code></td>
                  <td>Flowable Payload</td>
                  <td><code>Tensor</code>, <code>Tensor[rank=N]</code>, <code>Tensor[*, *]</code></td>
                  <td>Yes</td>
                  <td>Yes (Axis 0 / Batch)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Image</code></td>
                  <td>Flowable Payload</td>
                  <td><code>Image</code>, <code>Image[*, *, C]</code>, <code>Image[H, W, C]</code></td>
                  <td>Yes</td>
                  <td>Yes (Channel Axis)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Audio</code></td>
                  <td>Flowable Payload</td>
                  <td><code>Audio</code>, <code>Audio[*, *]</code>, <code>Audio[C, *]</code></td>
                  <td>Yes</td>
                  <td>Yes (Channel or Sample)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Scalar</code></td>
                  <td>Flowable Payload</td>
                  <td><code>Scalar</code> (Rank-0 numerical value)</td>
                  <td>Yes</td>
                  <td>No (Rank 0)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>RawBytes</code></td>
                  <td>Flowable Payload</td>
                  <td><code>RawBytes</code> (Opaque linear buffer)</td>
                  <td>Yes</td>
                  <td>No (Decode first)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Composite</code></td>
                  <td>Flowable Payload</td>
                  <td><code>Composite</code> (Tuple of payloads)</td>
                  <td>Yes</td>
                  <td>No</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>IntArg</code></td>
                  <td>Configuration Arg</td>
                  <td><code>IntArg</code> (Integer scalar parameter)</td>
                  <td>No (Action arg only)</td>
                  <td>No</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>FloatArg</code></td>
                  <td>Configuration Arg</td>
                  <td><code>FloatArg</code> (Float scalar parameter)</td>
                  <td>No (Action arg only)</td>
                  <td>No</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>StrArg</code></td>
                  <td>Configuration Arg</td>
                  <td><code>StrArg</code> (String scalar parameter)</td>
                  <td>No (Action arg only)</td>
                  <td>No</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>BoolArg</code></td>
                  <td>Configuration Arg</td>
                  <td><code>BoolArg</code> (Boolean scalar parameter)</td>
                  <td>No (Action arg only)</td>
                  <td>No</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 3.2: TENSOR -->
        <div id="types-tensor" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">3.2. Tensor (<code>Tensor</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Components:</strong> A contiguous dense multi-dimensional buffer, a shape array <code>[D_0, D_1, ..., D_k]</code>, memory strides, and a numeric element data type (<code>f32</code>, <code>u8</code>, or <code>i32</code>).
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Defining Shapes &amp; Dimensions:</strong> You can constrain tensor inputs with precise shapes or wildcard dimensions:
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Tensor Shape Annotations</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># 1. Unconstrained: Any rank and shape accepted</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Tensor</span> <span class="tok-var">$data</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 2. Fixed Rank: Enforces exactly rank 2 (matrix), dynamic dimensions</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Tensor[rank=2]</span> <span class="tok-var">$matrix</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 3. Dynamic Wildcard Dimensions: 2D tensor where both dimensions are dynamic</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Tensor[*, *]</span> <span class="tok-var">$table</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 4. Partial Fixed Dimensions: Dynamic batch size with fixed 512-dim embedding vector</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Tensor[*, 512]</span> <span class="tok-var">$embeddings</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 5. Static Fixed Shape: Exact 3x224x224 tensor dimensions</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Tensor[3, 224, 224]</span> <span class="tok-var">$batch</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>How <code>Tensor</code> Works with <code>each</code>:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="doc-list" style="margin: 0 0 16px 20px; color: var(--grey-800); line-height: 1.65;">
            <li><strong>Iteration Axis:</strong> Always iterates along <strong>Axis 0</strong> (the leading dimension / batch axis).</li>
            <li><strong>Iteration Count:</strong> Exactly <code>shape[0]</code> parallel iterations are spawned.</li>
            <li><strong>Loop Variable Derivation:</strong>
              <br />• If rank $\ge 2$: Each iteration produces an independent <code>Tensor</code> with rank reduced by one (<code>Tensor[rank=N-1]</code>). Slicing <code>Tensor[32, 128]</code> yields 32 parallel sub-flows each receiving a <code>Tensor[128]</code>.
              <br />• If rank 1: Iterating a 1D tensor slices single elements, binding each iteration to a <strong><code>Scalar</code></strong> (rank-0 numeric value).
              <br />• If rank 0: A rank-0 scalar tensor has no dimensions to slice and is rejected at compile time.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Restacking:</strong> Outputs from all iterations are collected and restacked along Axis 0 back into the parent tensor shape.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 3.3: IMAGE -->
        <div id="types-image" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">3.3. Image (<code>Image</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Components:</strong> A multi-channel pixel buffer, spatial height ($H$) and width ($W$), color channel count ($C$), color space metadata (<code>ColorSpace</code>: <code>rgb</code>, <code>rgba</code>, <code>grayscale</code>, <code>bgr</code>, <code>bgra</code>), and memory layout (<code>hwc</code> or <code>chw</code>, default <code>hwc</code>).
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Defining Shapes &amp; Dimensions:</strong>
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Image Shape Declarations</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># 1. Unconstrained: Any resolution and channel count</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Image</span> <span class="tok-var">$img_in</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 2. Dynamic resolution with fixed 3-channel RGB/BGR</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Image[*, *, 3]</span> <span class="tok-var">$rgb_in</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 3. Grayscale image with 1 channel</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Image[*, *, 1]</span> <span class="tok-var">$gray_in</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 4. Fixed static resolution and channel count</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Image[1080, 1920, 3]</span> <span class="tok-var">$frame</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>How <code>Image</code> Works with <code>each</code> (Channel Slicing):</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="doc-list" style="margin: 0 0 16px 20px; color: var(--grey-800); line-height: 1.65;">
            <li><strong>Iteration Axis:</strong> Crucially, <code>each</code> on an <code>Image</code> slices along the <strong>Color Channel Axis</strong> ($C$), <em>not</em> spatial rows or columns!
              <br />• In <code>hwc</code> layout: slices along <strong>Axis 2</strong>.
              <br />• In <code>chw</code> layout: slices along <strong>Axis 0</strong>.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Iteration Count:</strong> Exactly $C$ parallel workers (e.g. 3 for RGB, 4 for RGBA).</li>
            <li><strong>Loop Variable Derivation:</strong> Each parallel iteration receives an independent rank-2 <strong><code>Image</code></strong> in <code>ColorSpace::Grayscale</code>, preserving the full $H \times W$ spatial resolution. This allows applying filters, equalizations, or thresholding to individual channels simultaneously.</li>
            <li><strong>Payload Kind Preservation (<code>E009</code>):</strong> The sub-flow inside <code>each</code> must preserve the payload kind. You cannot convert the channel slice into a <code>Tensor</code> or <code>Audio</code> mid-loop without causing static error <code>E009</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Restacking:</strong> The transformed grayscale channel slices are reassembled along the channel axis back into the parent's original color space and layout.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 3.4: AUDIO -->
        <div id="types-audio" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">3.4. Audio (<code>Audio</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Components:</strong> A PCM sample buffer, channel count ($C$), sample count ($S$), sample rate in Hz (e.g. 44100, 48000), channel layout (<code>AudioChannelLayout</code>: <code>Mono</code>, <code>Stereo</code>, <code>Surround51</code>, etc.), and memory layout (<code>Planar</code> where channels are Axis 0 <code>[channels, samples]</code>, or <code>Interleaved</code> where channels are Axis 1 <code>[samples, channels]</code>).
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Defining Shapes &amp; Dimensions:</strong>
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Audio Declarations</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># 1. Unconstrained: Any channel count and duration</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Audio</span> <span class="tok-var">$audio_in</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 2. Dynamic 2D audio signal (channels x samples)</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Audio[*, *]</span> <span class="tok-var">$stream</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 3. Stereo audio (2 channels) with dynamic sample length</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Audio[2, *]</span> <span class="tok-var">$stereo</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># 4. Mono audio signal</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Audio[1, *]</span> <span class="tok-var">$mono</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>How <code>Audio</code> Works with <code>each</code>:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="doc-list" style="margin: 0 0 16px 20px; color: var(--grey-800); line-height: 1.65;">
            <li><strong>Multi-Channel Audio ($C &gt; 1$):</strong> Slices along the <strong>channel axis</strong> (Axis 0 in <code>Planar</code>, Axis 1 in <code>Interleaved</code>). Each parallel worker receives an independent single-channel <strong><code>Audio</code></strong> (mono) payload with the parent's sample rate intact. Slices are processed concurrently and restacked along the channel axis.</li>
            <li><strong>Mono Audio ($C = 1$, rank-1 <code>[samples]</code>):</strong> Slices along the <strong>sample axis</strong>. Each iteration receives a single sample as a <strong><code>Scalar</code></strong> float. Slices are restacked along the sample axis back into mono audio.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 3.5: SCALAR -->
        <div id="types-scalar" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">3.5. Scalar (<code>Scalar</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Components:</strong> A rank-0 numerical float or integer value (represented internally as a 0-dimensional tensor containing exactly 1 element).
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Defining Shape:</strong> <code>Scalar</code> has no dimensions (rank 0). It is declared simply as <code>accept Scalar $name [= default]</code>.
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>How <code>Scalar</code> Works with <code>each</code>:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="doc-list" style="margin: 0 0 16px 20px; color: var(--grey-800); line-height: 1.65;">
            <li><strong>Direct Iteration is Prohibited:</strong> A scalar has zero dimensions and cannot be the target of an <code>each</code> loop (<code>cannot loop over a scalar value; 'each' requires a rank &gt;= 1 payload</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>The Unit of 1D Slicing:</strong> <code>Scalar</code> is the payload yielded when iterating a 1D <code>Tensor</code> or a mono <code>Audio</code> stream. Inside the loop, it flows through scalar-capable math actions (e.g. <code>relu</code>, <code>abs</code>, <code>clamp</code>, <code>sin</code>) and is restacked into the original 1D tensor.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 3.6: RAWBYTES -->
        <div id="types-rawbytes" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">3.6. RawBytes (<code>RawBytes</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Components:</strong> An opaque contiguous linear byte buffer (<code>RVec&lt;u8&gt;</code>). It represents unparsed binary file data (e.g. WAV audio files with headers, encoded PNG/JPEG image files, or serialized payloads).
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Defining Shape:</strong> <code>RawBytes</code> has no shape or dimension concepts. It is declared as <code>accept RawBytes $data</code>.
          </p>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>How <code>RawBytes</code> Works with <code>each</code>:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="doc-list" style="margin: 0 0 16px 20px; color: var(--grey-800); line-height: 1.65;">
            <li><strong>Direct Iteration is Prohibited:</strong> You cannot loop over raw bytes (<code>Cannot execute 'each' on a raw-bytes payload; decode it into Tensor, Image, or Audio first</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Decode First:</strong> Pipe the raw bytes through an ingestion action (such as <code>to_audio</code> or <code>to_tensor</code>) before invoking <code>each</code> on the decoded stream.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 3.7: COMPOSITE -->
        <div id="types-composite" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">3.7. Composite (<code>Composite</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Components:</strong> A compound heterogeneous tuple combining multiple distinct payloads (e.g. paired audio and image streams, or feature tensors paired with metadata).
          </p>
          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Behavior with <code>each</code>:</strong> Composite payloads cannot be sliced directly by <code>each</code>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 3.8: CONFIGURATION ARGUMENTS -->
        <div id="types-arguments" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">3.8. Configuration Arguments (<code>IntArg</code>, <code>FloatArg</code>, <code>StrArg</code>, <code>BoolArg</code>)</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>Components:</strong> Strongly-typed primitive scalar arguments passed from host runtimes to configure action settings.
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Configuration Argument Types</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-comment"># Integer parameter (dimensions, sample rates, axis indices)</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">IntArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$target_w</span> = <span class="tok-num">512</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># Floating-point parameter (contrast, gain, threshold, sigma)</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">FloatArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$contrast</span> = <span class="tok-num">1.15</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># String parameter (color space formats, interpolation modes)</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">StrArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$filter</span> = <span class="tok-str">"bilinear"</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># Boolean flag (normalization, channel swapping)</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">BoolArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$normalize</span> = <span class="tok-keyword">true</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-callout">
            <strong>Non-Flowable Guarantee (<code>E007</code>):</strong> Configuration arguments cannot initiate a dataflow stream (e.g. <code>$target_w &gt;&gt; ...</code> raises <code>E007: cannot pipe from non-flowable argument type</code>). They are strictly passed to action calls (e.g. <code>resize(width=$target_w)</code>) and can be accessed as parameters inside <code>each</code> sub-flows.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 3.9: DEEP DIVE EACH -->
        <div id="types-each" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">3.9. Deep Dive: Slicing &amp; Restacking with <code>each</code></h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            The <code>each</code> operator is Morflow's parallel map-reduce construct. It dynamically slices a multi-dimensional payload across a specific axis, dispatches each slice independently across a multi-threaded Rayon work-stealing pool, and deterministically restacks the transformed slices back together in original sequence order.
          </p>

          <h4 class="doc-h3" style="font-size: 16px; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Slicing &amp; Restacking Semantics by Type</h4>
          <div class="doc-table-container">
            <table class="doc-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Incoming Payload</th>
                  <th>Iteration Axis</th>
                  <th>Loop Variable (<code>$var</code>) Type</th>
                  <th>Restacked Result</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Tensor[rank=N]</code> ($N \ge 2$)</td>
                  <td>Axis 0 (Batch / Leading)</td>
                  <td><code>Tensor[rank=N-1]</code></td>
                  <td><code>Tensor[rank=N]</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Tensor[rank=1]</code> (1D Vector)</td>
                  <td>Axis 0 (Elements)</td>
                  <td><code>Scalar</code></td>
                  <td><code>Tensor[rank=1]</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Image[H, W, C]</code> (HWC layout)</td>
                  <td>Axis 2 (Channel Axis)</td>
                  <td><code>Image[H, W, 1]</code> (Grayscale)</td>
                  <td><code>Image[H, W, C]</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Image[C, H, W]</code> (CHW layout)</td>
                  <td>Axis 0 (Channel Axis)</td>
                  <td><code>Image[1, H, W]</code> (Grayscale)</td>
                  <td><code>Image[C, H, W]</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Audio[C, S]</code> ($C &gt; 1$, Planar)</td>
                  <td>Axis 0 (Channel Axis)</td>
                  <td><code>Audio[1, S]</code> (Mono Audio)</td>
                  <td><code>Audio[C, S]</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>Audio[1, S]</code> (Mono Audio)</td>
                  <td>Axis 0 (Sample Axis)</td>
                  <td><code>Scalar</code> (Float sample)</td>
                  <td><code>Audio[1, S]</code></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h4 class="doc-h3" style="font-size: 16px; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 12px;">The Core Rules of <code>each</code></h4>
          <ul class="doc-list" style="margin: 0 0 16px 20px; color: var(--grey-800); line-height: 1.65;">
            <li>
              <strong>1. Payload Kind Invariant (<code>E009</code>):</strong> The sub-flow inside <code>each</code> must preserve the payload kind of the loop variable. If you iterate an <code>Image</code>, each parallel iteration receives a grayscale <code>Image</code> and must produce an <code>Image</code>. If a step inside the loop produces a <code>Tensor</code> or <code>Audio</code>, <code>morflow check</code> reports compile error <code>E009: 'each' body changes the payload kind</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>2. Prohibition of <code>emit</code> Inside Loops:</strong> Slices execute asynchronously and out-of-order across CPU cores. To maintain deterministic synchronization with host applications, direct emission (<code>emit</code>) inside an <code>each</code> block is strictly prohibited. Outputs must be emitted downstream after the loop has restacked all slices.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>3. Single Static Assignment (SSA) Safety:</strong> The loop variable (e.g. <code>$channel</code>) is immutable within its iteration scope. Intermediate variables tapped inside an <code>each</code> loop cannot conflict with external flows.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>4. External Parameter Access:</strong> Sub-flows inside <code>each</code> can freely reference external variables and configuration arguments declared in the outer scope (e.g. <code>$channel &gt;&gt; biquad_filter(freq=$cutoff)</code>).
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Parallel Multi-Channel Audio Loop</span>
              <span>morf</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-keyword">import</span> audio_essentials/latest

<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Audio</span> <span class="tok-var">$stereo_audio</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">FloatArg</span> <span class="tok-var">$cutoff_freq</span> = <span class="tok-num">120.0</span>

<span class="tok-comment"># Stereo audio ($stereo_audio has 2 channels)</span>
<span class="tok-comment"># 'each' slices the channel axis, running 2 parallel workers on Rayon</span>
<span class="tok-var">$stereo_audio</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-keyword">each</span> (<span class="tok-var">$channel</span>) &#123;
        <span class="tok-comment"># $channel is a mono Audio payload</span>
        <span class="tok-var">$channel</span>
            <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">biquad_filter</span>(<span class="tok-param">type</span>=<span class="tok-str">"highpass"</span>, <span class="tok-param">freq</span>=<span class="tok-var">$cutoff_freq</span>)
            <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">compressor</span>(<span class="tok-param">threshold_db</span>=<span class="tok-num">-12.0</span>, <span class="tok-param">ratio</span>=<span class="tok-num">3.0</span>)
    &#125;
    <span class="tok-comment"># Processed channels are restacked into stereo Audio</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">stereo_widen</span>(<span class="tok-param">width</span>=<span class="tok-num">1.2</span>)
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">to_wav</span>
    <span class="tok-op">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="tok-fn">emit</span></code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 4: PIPELINE EXECUTION -->
      <section id="exec" class="doc-section">
        <div class="doc-section-header">
          <p class="badge">Section 4</p>
          <h2 class="doc-h2">4. Pipeline Execution</h2>
          <p class="doc-p">
            Execute compiled <code>.morf</code> dataflow graphs natively across languages with zero train-serve skew. Morflow provides idiomatic host SDKs for Python, JavaScript/Node.js, Java, and Rust, mapping host tensors, image arrays, and raw binary streams directly into the engine's execution graph.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 4.1: PYTHON -->
        <div id="exec-python" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">4.1. Python</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            The Python SDK (<code>morflow</code>) integrates directly with NumPy arrays, raw bytes, and file streams with zero-copy buffer sharing into the underlying engine. Payloads can be passed as typed wrappers (<code>morflow.Image</code>, <code>morflow.Audio</code>, <code>morflow.Tensor</code>), or plain NumPy arrays and bytes matching declared <code>accept</code> types.
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Installation</span>
              <span>Shell</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code>pip install morflow</code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Typed Execution &amp; Positional Arguments in Python</span>
              <span>python</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-keyword">import</span> numpy <span class="tok-keyword">as</span> np
<span class="tok-keyword">from</span> PIL <span class="tok-keyword">import</span> Image
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> morflow

<span class="tok-comment"># 1. Load pipeline from file</span>
pipeline = morflow.<span class="tok-fn">load</span>(<span class="tok-str">"image_pipeline.morf"</span>)

<span class="tok-comment"># 2. Pass NumPy array wrapped as morflow.Image</span>
img = Image.<span class="tok-fn">open</span>(<span class="tok-str">"input.png"</span>).<span class="tok-fn">convert</span>(<span class="tok-str">"RGB"</span>)
np_img = np.<span class="tok-fn">array</span>(img, dtype=np.uint8)

<span class="tok-comment"># 3. Execute with positional arguments (payload, target_w, target_h)</span>
<span class="tok-comment"># Declared defaults (512, 512) apply if arguments are omitted: pipeline.run(payload)</span>
result_np = pipeline.<span class="tok-fn">run</span>(morflow.<span class="tok-fn">Image</span>(np_img, color=<span class="tok-str">"rgb"</span>), <span class="tok-num">512</span>, <span class="tok-num">512</span>)

<span class="tok-comment"># 4. Save result</span>
out_img = Image.<span class="tok-fn">fromarray</span>(result_np)
out_img.<span class="tok-fn">save</span>(<span class="tok-str">"output.png"</span>)

<span class="tok-comment"># ----------------------------------------------------</span>
<span class="tok-comment"># Audio Processing (Pass and receive raw WAV bytes)</span>
<span class="tok-comment"># ----------------------------------------------------</span>
audio_pipe = morflow.<span class="tok-fn">load</span>(<span class="tok-str">"audio_pipeline.morf"</span>)
<span class="tok-keyword">with</span> <span class="tok-fn">open</span>(<span class="tok-str">"input.wav"</span>, <span class="tok-str">"rb"</span>) <span class="tok-keyword">as</span> f:
    input_bytes = f.<span class="tok-fn">read</span>()

<span class="tok-comment"># Pass raw bytes (bound to accept RawBytes) and custom sample rate IntArg</span>
output_wav_bytes = audio_pipe.<span class="tok-fn">run</span>(input_bytes, <span class="tok-num">44100</span>)
<span class="tok-keyword">with</span> <span class="tok-fn">open</span>(<span class="tok-str">"output.wav"</span>, <span class="tok-str">"wb"</span>) <span class="tok-keyword">as</span> f:
    f.<span class="tok-fn">write</span>(output_wav_bytes)</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 4.2: JAVASCRIPT / NODE.JS -->
        <div id="exec-js" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">4.2. JavaScript / Node.js</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            The Node.js SDK provides asynchronous execution (via <code>pipeline.run()</code> or <code>pipeline.runArgs()</code> offloading work to a background worker pool) and synchronous execution (via <code>pipeline.runSync()</code> / <code>pipeline.runSyncArgs()</code>). Positional arguments matching declared <code>accept</code> statements can be passed directly as heterogeneous arguments (numbers, booleans, strings, Buffers, or <code>TensorInput</code>).
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Installation</span>
              <span>Shell</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code>npm install morflow</code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Async Pipeline Execution with Arguments in Node.js</span>
              <span>javascript</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-keyword">import</span> fs <span class="tok-keyword">from</span> <span class="tok-str">'node:fs'</span>;
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> morflow <span class="tok-keyword">from</span> <span class="tok-str">'morflow'</span>;

<span class="tok-comment">// 1. Load pipeline from file</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">const</span> pipeline = morflow.<span class="tok-fn">load</span>(<span class="tok-str">'image_pipeline.morf'</span>);

<span class="tok-comment">// 2. Construct TensorInput with explicit payloadType</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">const</span> inputBuffer = fs.<span class="tok-fn">readFileSync</span>(<span class="tok-str">'input_raw_rgb.bin'</span>);
<span class="tok-keyword">const</span> tensorInput = &#123;
  data: inputBuffer,
  shape: [<span class="tok-num">1080</span>, <span class="tok-num">1920</span>, <span class="tok-num">3</span>],
  dtype: <span class="tok-str">'u8'</span>,
  payloadType: <span class="tok-str">'image'</span>,
  colorSpace: <span class="tok-str">'rgb'</span>
&#125;;

<span class="tok-comment">// 3. Run asynchronously on worker pool with positional arguments (runArgs)</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">const</span> outputTensor = <span class="tok-keyword">await</span> pipeline.<span class="tok-fn">runArgs</span>(tensorInput, <span class="tok-num">512</span>, <span class="tok-num">512</span>);

console.<span class="tok-fn">log</span>(<span class="tok-str">`Shape: $&#123;outputTensor.shape&#125;, Dtype: $&#123;outputTensor.dtype&#125;`</span>);
<span class="tok-keyword">const</span> outBuffer = outputTensor.<span class="tok-fn">toBuffer</span>();
fs.<span class="tok-fn">writeFileSync</span>(<span class="tok-str">'output_raw_rgba.bin'</span>, outBuffer);

<span class="tok-comment">// ----------------------------------------------------</span>
<span class="tok-comment">// Audio DSP Execution (Direct Buffer &amp; Argument I/O)</span>
<span class="tok-comment">// ----------------------------------------------------</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">const</span> audioPipe = morflow.<span class="tok-fn">load</span>(<span class="tok-str">'audio_pipeline.morf'</span>);
<span class="tok-keyword">const</span> wavBuffer = fs.<span class="tok-fn">readFileSync</span>(<span class="tok-str">'input.wav'</span>);

<span class="tok-comment">// Execute asynchronously with buffer and sample rate argument</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">const</span> outWav = <span class="tok-keyword">await</span> audioPipe.<span class="tok-fn">runArgs</span>(wavBuffer, <span class="tok-num">44100</span>);
fs.<span class="tok-fn">writeFileSync</span>(<span class="tok-str">'output.wav'</span>, outWav.<span class="tok-fn">toBuffer</span>());</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 4.3: JAVA -->
        <div id="exec-java" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">4.3. Java</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            The Java SDK wraps native JNI bindings with type-safe classes, automatic memory cleanup, and direct tensor buffers for high-throughput enterprise JVM backends. Positional parameters are bound using <code>pipeline.runArgs(...)</code>.
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Maven Dependency (pom.xml)</span>
              <span>XML</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.morflow&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;morflow&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;0.2.0&lt;/version&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Pipeline Execution in Java</span>
              <span>java</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-keyword">import</span> org.morflow.Morflow;
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> org.morflow.Pipeline;
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> org.morflow.MorflowTensor;
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> java.nio.file.Files;
<span class="tok-keyword">import</span> java.nio.file.Path;

<span class="tok-keyword">public class</span> <span class="tok-fn">MorflowRunner</span> &#123;
    <span class="tok-keyword">public static void</span> <span class="tok-fn">main</span>(String[] args) <span class="tok-keyword">throws</span> Exception &#123;
        <span class="tok-comment">// 1. Load pipeline</span>
        <span class="tok-keyword">try</span> (Pipeline pipeline = Morflow.<span class="tok-fn">load</span>(<span class="tok-str">"image_pipeline.morf"</span>)) &#123;
            <span class="tok-comment">// 2. Wrap image bytes into MorflowTensor [H, W, C]</span>
            <span class="tok-keyword">byte</span>[] rgbBytes = Files.<span class="tok-fn">readAllBytes</span>(Path.<span class="tok-fn">of</span>(<span class="tok-str">"input_rgb.raw"</span>));
            MorflowTensor inputTensor = MorflowTensor.<span class="tok-fn">fromByteArray</span>(
                rgbBytes,
                <span class="tok-keyword">new int</span>[]&#123;<span class="tok-num">1080</span>, <span class="tok-num">1920</span>, <span class="tok-num">3</span>&#125;
            );

            <span class="tok-comment">// 3. Execute pipeline with positional arguments (runArgs)</span>
            <span class="tok-keyword">try</span> (MorflowTensor outputTensor = pipeline.<span class="tok-fn">runArgs</span>(inputTensor, <span class="tok-num">512</span>, <span class="tok-num">512</span>)) &#123;
                <span class="tok-keyword">int</span>[] outShape = outputTensor.<span class="tok-fn">getShape</span>();
                <span class="tok-keyword">byte</span>[] outBytes = outputTensor.<span class="tok-fn">toByteArray</span>();
                Files.<span class="tok-fn">write</span>(Path.<span class="tok-fn">of</span>(<span class="tok-str">"output.raw"</span>), outBytes);
            &#125;
        &#125;

        <span class="tok-comment">// Audio WAV execution with raw byte array and sample rate argument</span>
        <span class="tok-keyword">try</span> (Pipeline audioPipe = Morflow.<span class="tok-fn">load</span>(<span class="tok-str">"audio_pipeline.morf"</span>)) &#123;
            <span class="tok-keyword">byte</span>[] inputWav = Files.<span class="tok-fn">readAllBytes</span>(Path.<span class="tok-fn">of</span>(<span class="tok-str">"input.wav"</span>));
            MorflowTensor audioOut = audioPipe.<span class="tok-fn">runArgs</span>(inputWav, <span class="tok-num">44100</span>);
            Files.<span class="tok-fn">write</span>(Path.<span class="tok-fn">of</span>(<span class="tok-str">"output.wav"</span>), audioOut.<span class="tok-fn">toByteArray</span>());
        &#125;
    &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 4.4: RUST -->
        <div id="exec-rust" class="doc-section">
          <h3 class="doc-h3">4.4. Rust</h3>
          <p class="doc-p">
            The native Rust engine crate (<code>morflow</code>) provides direct access to <code>Payload</code> variants (<code>Image</code>, <code>Audio</code>, <code>Tensor</code>, <code>Data</code>, <code>Scalar</code>) with compile-time type safety and zero runtime overhead.
          </p>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Cargo Dependencies</span>
              <span>Shell</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code>cargo add morflow</code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-code-card">
            <div class="doc-code-header">
              <span>Native Pipeline Execution in Rust</span>
              <span>rust</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-code-pre"><code><span class="tok-keyword">use</span> core_types::&#123;ColorSpace, Image, Payload, RVec&#125;;
<span class="tok-keyword">use</span> morflow::Morflow;
<span class="tok-keyword">use</span> std::fs;

<span class="tok-keyword">fn</span> <span class="tok-fn">main</span>() -&gt; Result&lt;(), Box&lt;<span class="tok-keyword">dyn</span> std::error::Error&gt;&gt; &#123;
    <span class="tok-comment">// 1. Load pipeline from file</span>
    <span class="tok-keyword">let mut</span> pipeline = Morflow::<span class="tok-fn">load</span>(<span class="tok-str">"image_pipeline.morf"</span>)?;

    <span class="tok-comment">// 2. Wrap image buffer into a Morflow Image payload</span>
    <span class="tok-keyword">let</span> img = image::<span class="tok-fn">open</span>(<span class="tok-str">"input.png"</span>)?.<span class="tok-fn">to_rgb8</span>();
    <span class="tok-keyword">let</span> input = Image::<span class="tok-fn">from_u8_hwc</span>(
        &amp;img,
        img.<span class="tok-fn">width</span>() <span class="tok-keyword">as</span> usize,
        img.<span class="tok-fn">height</span>() <span class="tok-keyword">as</span> usize,
        ColorSpace::Rgb,
    ).<span class="tok-fn">map_err</span>(|e| e.<span class="tok-fn">to_string</span>())?;

    <span class="tok-comment">// 3. Execute Morflow pipeline with declared payload</span>
    <span class="tok-keyword">let</span> outputs = pipeline.<span class="tok-fn">run</span>(Payload::Image(input))?;

    <span class="tok-comment">// 4. Extract emitted payload and save output</span>
    <span class="tok-keyword">if let</span> Payload::Image(out) = outputs.<span class="tok-fn">into_single</span>()? &#123;
        <span class="tok-keyword">let</span> bytes = out.<span class="tok-fn">to_contiguous_bytes</span>();
        image::<span class="tok-fn">save_buffer</span>(
            <span class="tok-str">"output.png"</span>,
            bytes.<span class="tok-fn">as_slice</span>(),
            out.<span class="tok-fn">width</span>() <span class="tok-keyword">as</span> u32,
            out.<span class="tok-fn">height</span>() <span class="tok-keyword">as</span> u32,
            image::ColorType::Rgba8,
        )?;
    &#125;

    <span class="tok-comment">// ----------------------------------------------------</span>
    <span class="tok-comment">// Audio DSP Execution (Direct Data Payload)</span>
    <span class="tok-comment">// ----------------------------------------------------</span>
    <span class="tok-keyword">let mut</span> audio_pipe = Morflow::<span class="tok-fn">load</span>(<span class="tok-str">"audio_pipeline.morf"</span>)?;
    <span class="tok-keyword">let</span> wav_bytes = fs::<span class="tok-fn">read</span>(<span class="tok-str">"input.wav"</span>)?;

    <span class="tok-keyword">let</span> audio_out = audio_pipe.<span class="tok-fn">run</span>(Payload::Data &#123;
        buffer: RVec::<span class="tok-fn">from</span>(wav_bytes),
    &#125;)?;

    <span class="tok-keyword">if let</span> Payload::Data &#123; buffer &#125; = audio_out.into_single()? &#123;
        fs::write(<span class="tok-str">"output.wav"</span>, buffer.as_slice())?;
    &#125;

    Ok(())
&#125;</code></pre>
